preConditionHook:
// LET THE FIRST PULLBACK TO THE ENTRY PRICE GO, EXIT AT BREAKEVEN ON THE SECOND.
// Once price has touched the entry price, moved away in the trade's favour by
// awayTicks, and come back to the entry price again, the trade is done: Brooks
// does not want it coming back a second time.
//
// Distinct from BreakevenStop, which arms on a dollar peak profit and exits on the
// FIRST return to entry, and from BreakevenRetestExit, which is the unarmed first
// touch. Both fire on the first return; this one cannot fire before the third leg
// of a touch-recover-touch sequence.
//
// THE FILL BAR'S TOUCH DOES NOT COUNT. The fill is at the bar's open, so
// low[0] <= ctx.EntryPrice() holds on the entry bar by construction (low <= open
// always) and an ungated rule would count it as the first test, degenerating to
// "exit on the first return after moving away" -- i.e. BreakevenStop. The touch
// test is therefore gated on ctx.BarsSinceEntry() >= 1.
//
// THE TWO FLAGS ARE PER POSITION, reset on ctx.BarsSinceEntry() == 0 -- VERIFIED
// as 0 on the fill bar and as restarting through a reversal, which a
// ctx.MarketPosition() == 0 reset would miss because a reversal never passes
// through flat. ORDER IS PART OF THE SPECIFICATION: the recovery is only recorded
// once a touch is on the books, the exit flag is computed before this bar's touch
// is recorded, and a single bar spanning both the entry price and
// entry + awayTicks therefore records the touch only, never the recovery as well.
// The exit is a local bool computed here rather than a postConditionHook update,
// so both twins evaluate the state machine in one place and in one order.
//
// The ctx.MarketPosition() guard is load-bearing, not decoration: ctx.EntryPrice()
// is 0.0 when flat and a back-adjusted price can be negative.
//
// V15-13's tick offset wins over T18-24's "new N-bar high" as the recovery test:
// it needs no Highest call site and it measures what Brooks is describing,
// distance from the stop.
//
// Ticks: MinMove/PriceScale are VERIFIED and the tick is written division-first,
// awayTicks * (ctx.MinMove() / ctx.PriceScale()), into a local.
//
// Every scratch value is a localVariables entry, never a hook-scope declaration,
// so the hooks survive a double placement.
//
// Deepest bar touched: 0.
tickSize = ctx.MinMove() / ctx.PriceScale();
if (ctx.BarsSinceEntry() == 0) {
    touchedLong = false;
    touchedShort = false;
    awayLong = false;
    awayShort = false;
}
atEntryLong = el_gt(ctx.MarketPosition(), 0) && ctx.BarsSinceEntry() >= 1 && el_le(low[0], ctx.EntryPrice());
atEntryShort = el_lt(ctx.MarketPosition(), 0) && ctx.BarsSinceEntry() >= 1 && el_ge(high[0], ctx.EntryPrice());
if (touchedLong && el_ge(high[0], ctx.EntryPrice() + awayTicks * tickSize)) awayLong = true;
if (touchedShort && el_le(low[0], ctx.EntryPrice() - awayTicks * tickSize)) awayShort = true;
secondTestLong = atEntryLong && touchedLong && awayLong;
secondTestShort = atEntryShort && touchedShort && awayShort;
if (atEntryLong) touchedLong = true;
if (atEntryShort) touchedShort = true;
